#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inverse_fourier_sin_transform

#% text
# `inverse_fourier_sin_transform(g, w, t)` gives the inverse sine transform `sqrt(2/pi) integrate(g*sin(w*t), [w, 0, inf])` of `g`, for `t > 0`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The same integral as `fourier_sin_transform`, with the variables exchanged.

#% item
# `fourier_parameters: [a, b]` gives `2 sqrt(abs(b)/(2 pi)^(1 + a)) integrate(g*sin(b*w*t), [w, 0, inf])`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
inverse_fourier_sin_transform(w/(w^2 + 1), w, t)
#% output
#= (1/2)*2^(1/2)*exp(-t)*pi^(1/2)

#% cell
inverse_fourier_sin_transform(exp(-w), w, t)
#% output
#= t*2^(1/2)*(pi^-1)^(1/2)/(1 + t^2)

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% cell
inverse_fourier_sin_transform(fourier_sin_transform(exp(-t), t, w), w, t)
#% output
#= exp(-t)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `fourier_sin_transform`, `inverse_fourier_cos_transform`
